  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is the dominant RNA encoder (0.725 best vs 0.586 for pca, 0.520 for scgpt), multiprofile is essential (0.725 vs 0.537 singleprofile), transformer aggregation outperforms avgpool (+0.019), and imagenet_vit_l slightly edges resnet50 (+0.012). The current best (config_008, 0.7250) already combines all top choices. Among untested configs, config_004 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + concat, multiprofile) is the highest-expected-accuracy option, as it retains the two strongest factors (scvi_n200, transformer) and only substitutes resnet50 for imagenet_vit_l and concat for weighted. Expected accuracy ~0.71 (extrapolating from config_013 at 0.713 with weighted and config_019 at 0.721 with concat). This is the last experiment; while it is unlikely to surpass 0.7250, it is the most logical exploitation of the scvi_n200+transformer family and tests whether the resnet50+concat combination might produce a synergistic effect. Expected relative cost: moderate, ~5–6 GPU hours (resnet50 adds ~2.5 hrs over ViT-L, concat slightly cheaper than weighted), bringing total to ~49 GPU hours."
}

